 R←TestSkyAt;m;b;same;obs;o;sky;members;map;pair;before;names;run;stmt
⍝ SkyAt takes stated day number, stated time (UTC hours), latitude and
⍝ longitude, and returns a namespace holding what the book's ENTRY,
⍝ CALCULATEPLANETS and CALCULATESTARS leave in globals, without setting
⍝ any globals itself. Each member equals the book's global exactly.
 m←## ⋄ b←##.Data ⋄ R←1
 same←{(⊃⍵)≡2⊃⍵:1 ⋄ 0⊣⎕←'FAIL: TestSkyAt: ',⍺}

⍝ Sky member ←→ book global after CALCULATEPLANETS then CALCULATESTARS
⍝ The book sets AAE twice: visible planets' alt/az, then bright stars'
 map←('StatedDayNo' 'STATEDDAYNO')('StatedTime' 'STATEDTIME')('Lat' 'LAT')('Long' 'LONG')
 map,←('Time' 'TIME')('Date' 'DATE')
 map,←('Planets' 'PLANETS')('PlanetsAA' 'PLANETAA')('PlanetsVisible' 'VP')
 map,←('PlanetCoord' 'PLANETCOORD')('Phase' 'PHASE')
 map,←('StarsVisible' 'VE')('BrightVisible' 'BRIGHTVIS')('BrightStarsAA' 'AAE')('StarCoord' 'STARCOORD')
 members←(⊃¨map),⊂'VisiblePlanetsAA'

⍝ Observations: (month day year) hour lat long
⍝ Anaheim 1974 (the book tests' case), Kohoutek within 100 days of
⍝ perihelion and outside it, southern hemisphere, near midnight
 obs←⊂(5 16 1974)5 33.767 ¯117.833
 obs,←⊂(1 10 1974)18 51.5 ¯0.13
 obs,←⊂(6 1 1973)2.5 40.7 ¯74
 obs,←⊂(12 25 1975)10 ¯33.87 151.21
 obs,←⊂(3 21 2000)23.9 0 0

 run←'STATEDDAYNO←JNU⊃OBS' 'STATEDTIME LAT LONG←1↓OBS'
 run,←'TIME←LONG TIMEADJUST STATEDTIME' 'DATE←STATEDDAYNO+(TIME÷24)-LONG÷360'
 run,←'CALCULATEPLANETS' 'PLANETVISAA←AAE' 'CALCULATESTARS'   ⍝ as EXAMPLE_RENDER, then WORK
 before←m.⎕NL ¯2 ¯9
 :For o :In obs
     sky←m.SkyAt(b.JNU⊃o),1↓o
     :If 9≠⎕NC'sky'
         ⎕←'FAIL: TestSkyAt: result is not a namespace' ⋄ R←0 ⋄ :Continue
     :EndIf
     names←sky.⎕NL ¯2
     R∧←('members ',⍕⊃o)same(members[⍋↑members])(names[⍋↑names])
     b.OBS←o
     :For stmt :In run
         b⍎stmt
     :EndFor
     :For pair :In map
         R∧←((⊃pair),' ',⍕⊃o)same(sky⍎⊃pair)(b⍎2⊃pair)
     :EndFor
     R∧←('VisiblePlanetsAA ',⍕⊃o)same sky.VisiblePlanetsAA b.PLANETVISAA
 :EndFor
 R∧←'comet in range: 11 objects'same 11(≢(m.SkyAt(b.JNU 1 10 1974)18 51.5 ¯0.13).PlanetsVisible)
 R∧←'comet out of range: 10 objects'same 10(≢(m.SkyAt(b.JNU 6 1 1973)2.5 40.7 ¯74).PlanetsVisible)
 R∧←'no globals set'same before(m.⎕NL ¯2 ¯9)
 b.⎕EX'OBS' 'PLANETVISAA'

 :If R
     ⎕←'PASS: TestSkyAt (',(⍕≢obs),' observations, ',(⍕≢members),' members)'
 :EndIf
